/**
 * @page py_sinter Sinter Integration (QEC Sampling)
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section py_sinter_overview Overview
 *
 * Maestro provides seamless integration with [Stim](https://github.com/quantumlib/Stim) and
 * [Sinter](https://github.com/quantumlib/Stim/tree/main/glue/sinter), the standard Python
 * benchmarking frameworks for quantum error correction (QEC).
 *
 * Through `maestro.sinter`, you can execute Stim circuits and error correction benchmarks
 * using Maestro's high-performance simulation engines (such as Matrix Product State or
 * GPU-accelerated statevectors) as custom Sinter samplers.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section py_sinter_install Installation
 *
 * To use the Sinter integration, install the optional `sinter` extra:
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * pip install "qoro-maestro[sinter]"
 * @endcode
 *
 * This installs `sinter>=1.14` and `stim>=1.14`.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section py_sinter_classes Core Classes and Functions
 *
 * | Class / Function | Description |
 * |------------------|-------------|
 * | `MaestroSinterSampler` | Implements `sinter.Sampler`. Passed to `sinter.collect()` as a custom sampler backend. |
 * | `MaestroCompiledSampler` | Implements `sinter.CompiledSampler`. Holds compiled circuit execution plans for repeated batch sampling. |
 * | `translate_stim_to_maestro(circuit)` | Converts a Stim circuit or circuit string into a Maestro `QuantumCircuit`. |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section py_sinter_example_collect Using with Sinter Collect
 *
 * You can pass `MaestroSinterSampler` into `sinter.collect` via the `custom_samplers` dictionary:
 *
 * @code{.py}
 * import sinter
 * import stim
 * from maestro.sinter import MaestroSinterSampler
 * import maestro
 *
 * # 1. Define a Stim surface code circuit
 * surface_code_task = sinter.Task(
 *     circuit=stim.Circuit.generated(
 *         "surface_code:rotated_memory_z",
 *         rounds=3,
 *         distance=3,
 *         after_clifford_depolarization=0.001,
 *     ),
 *     json_metadata={"d": 3, "r": 3, "p": 0.001},
 * )
 *
 * # 2. Configure Maestro backend options (e.g. Matrix Product State)
 * mps_config = maestro.SimulatorConfig(
 *     simulation_type=maestro.SimulationType.MatrixProductState,
 *     max_bond_dimension=64,
 * )
 *
 * # 3. Instantiate Maestro custom sampler
 * custom_samplers = {
 *     "maestro": MaestroSinterSampler(config=mps_config)
 * }
 *
 * # 4. Collect error correction statistics
 * stats = sinter.collect(
 *     num_workers=4,
 *     max_shots=100_000,
 *     max_errors=100,
 *     tasks=[surface_code_task],
 *     decoders=["pymatching"],
 *     custom_samplers=custom_samplers,
 * )
 *
 * for sample in stats:
 *     print(f"Errors: {sample.errors} / {sample.shots} (rate: {sample.errors / sample.shots:.4e})")
 * @endcode
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section py_sinter_example_compiled Direct Sampling with MaestroCompiledSampler
 *
 * For direct shot sampling from Python without running a full Sinter task collection:
 *
 * @code{.py}
 * import stim
 * from maestro.sinter import MaestroCompiledSampler
 * import maestro
 *
 * circuit = stim.Circuit("""
 *     H 0
 *     CX 0 1
 *     M 0 1
 *     DETECTOR(0, 0) rec[-1] rec[-2]
 * """)
 *
 * sampler = MaestroCompiledSampler(circuit)
 *
 * # Sample detection events and observable flips as numpy boolean arrays
 * det_samples, obs_samples = sampler.sample(shots=1000)
 * print("Detection events shape:", det_samples.shape)  # (1000, num_detectors)
 * print("Observable flips shape:", obs_samples.shape)  # (1000, num_observables)
 * @endcode
 */
